{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for which read and delivered marks a device sends, and how often. The wire is in receipt.json.",
    "Normative: docs/sealed-messages.md §Receipts (the Routing rules).",
    "Every mark goes to every device in the conversation, the sender's own included, like any other send, so its recipients say nothing about who wrote the messages it covers. Nothing about a mark depends on whom the sender blocked; the table therefore has no recipients, authors or block list.",
    "`read.trail` is the frame ids of the transcript the caller holds, in ascending order. A read goes when `m` is not empty and differs from `sentRead`, unless `m` and `sentRead` are both in the trail and `sentRead` is at or after `m`.",
    "A delivered mark goes when `m` is not empty and differs from `sentDelivered`, unless a read covers it. The covering read is the read sent in the same flush, else `sentRead`; it covers the delivered message when it names the same message, or when both are in `read.trail` and the delivered message is at or before it.",
    "`lane`, when present and not null, is the envelope id of the newest reaction, edit or delete from somebody else opened since the last flush. When nothing else goes, one lane mark naming it goes, written in `want` as {k: \"delivered\", m, l: true} and sent as `k: \"lane\"` (receipt.json). It is never checked against `sentDelivered` or a read, and it moves neither. When anything else goes, that is the batch's one follow-up.",
    "The read is sent first, then the delivered mark. `want` is the list of sends, in order, as {k, m} or {k, m, l}.",
    "`spacing` pins the least wait between two flushes into one conversation: min(`maxMs`, max(`baseMs`, devices × `perDeviceMs`)), where devices is the number of leaves in the tree when the last flush went. The first mark into a conversation waits `baseMs`.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
